    "crmInstructions": {
      "zapier": "1. Go to zapier.com → \"Create Zap\"\n2. Trigger: \"Webhooks by Zapier\" → \"Catch Hook\"\n3. Copy the generated URL and paste it above\n4. Action: connect to your favorite CRM (HubSpot, Salesforce, etc.)",
      "make": "1. Go to make.com → \"Create a new scenario\"\n2. Add the \"Webhooks\" module → \"Custom Webhook\"\n3. Copy the generated URL and paste it above\n4. Connect to your CRM in the next module",
      "gohighlevel": "1. Go to Settings → Integrations → Webhooks\n2. Click \"Add Webhook\"\n3. Paste the ZyraVoice URL\n4. Select the events: Contact Created, Call Ended",
      "hubspot": "1. Go to Settings → Integrations → Private Apps\n2. Create an app and copy the Webhook URL\n3. Or use Zapier/Make as an intermediary for more flexibility",
      "monday": "1. Go to your Board → Integrations → Webhooks\n2. Create an incoming webhook\n3. Copy the generated URL and paste it above",
      "airtable": "1. Airtable has no direct native webhooks\n2. Use Make or Zapier as an intermediary\n3. In Make: \"Airtable\" module → \"Create a Record\"\n4. In Zapier: Action → Airtable → \"Create Record\"",
      "notion": "1. Notion has no native webhooks\n2. Use Make or Zapier as an intermediary\n3. In Make: \"Notion\" module → \"Create a Database Item\"\n4. In Zapier: Action → Notion → \"Create Database Item\"",
      "pipedrive": "1. Go to Tools → Webhooks → \"Add Webhook\"\n2. Or use Zapier for more flexibility\n3. Copy the URL and paste it above",
      "salesforce": "1. Use Zapier or Make as an intermediary\n2. In Zapier: Action → Salesforce → \"Create Record\"\n3. Map the fields from the ZyraVoice payload",
      "n8n": "1. Create a workflow → \"Add first step\" → \"On webhook call\"\n2. Copy the generated webhook URL\n3. Paste it above and connect to your CRM in the next node",
      "custom": "Your server will receive a POST with a ZyraVoice JSON payload.\nVerify authenticity with the X-ZyraVoice-Signature header (HMAC SHA-256).\nExample: X-ZyraVoice-Signature: sha256=<hex>"
